        "prompt": "Determine how many paths start and finish at $(0,0)$ given that they have length:",
        "layout": "grid",
        "columns": 2,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p13-q12-a",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "a",
            "prompt": "$2$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$4$",
              "worked": "The steps must be one N and one S, or one E and one W.\n$$\\begin{align*}T_2&=\\frac{2!}{1!1!}+\\frac{2!}{1!1!}\\\\T_2&=2+2\\\\T_2&=4.\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 24
          },
          {
            "id": "p13-q12-b",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "b",
            "prompt": "$4$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$36$",
              "worked": "Returning to the origin requires equal numbers of N and S steps, and equal numbers of E and W steps. The counts $(N,S,E,W)$ are $(0,0,2,2)$, $(1,1,1,1)$ or $(2,2,0,0)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}T_4&=\\frac{4!}{2!2!}+\\frac{4!}{1!1!1!1!}+\\frac{4!}{2!2!}\\\\T_4&=6+24+6\\\\T_4&=36.\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 40
          },
          {
            "id": "p13-q12-c",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "c",
            "prompt": "$6$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": {
                "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
                "version": 1,
                "blocks": [
                  {
                    "id": "p13-q12-c-short-result",
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "fontSize": null,
                    "align": "left",
                    "spaceBefore": 0,
                    "spaceAfter": 2,
                    "lineHeight": 1.4,
                    "indent": 0,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "type": "math",
                        "latex": "400",
                        "display": false
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "p13-q12-c-short-method",
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "fontSize": null,
                    "align": "left",
                    "spaceBefore": 0,
                    "spaceAfter": 2,
                    "lineHeight": 1.4,
                    "indent": 0,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Sum repeated-direction arrangements over all balanced step counts.",
                        "marks": []
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              "worked": "Let there be $k$ N steps and $k$ S steps. There must then be $3-k$ E steps and $3-k$ W steps, where $k=0,1,2,3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}T_6&=2\\left(\\frac{6!}{3!3!}\\right)+2\\left(\\frac{6!}{1!1!2!2!}\\right)\\\\T_6&=2(20)+2(180)\\\\T_6&=400.\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 50
          },
          {
            "id": "p13-q12-d",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "d",
            "prompt": "$8$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": {
                "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
                "version": 1,
                "blocks": [
                  {
                    "id": "p13-q12-d-short-result",
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "fontSize": null,
                    "align": "left",
                    "spaceBefore": 0,
                    "spaceAfter": 2,
                    "lineHeight": 1.4,
                    "indent": 0,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "type": "math",
                        "latex": "4900",
                        "display": false
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "p13-q12-d-short-method",
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "fontSize": null,
                    "align": "left",
                    "spaceBefore": 0,
                    "spaceAfter": 2,
                    "lineHeight": 1.4,
                    "indent": 0,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Sum repeated-direction arrangements over all balanced step counts.",
                        "marks": []
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              "worked": "Let there be $k$ N steps and $k$ S steps. There must then be $4-k$ E steps and $4-k$ W steps, where $k=0,1,2,3,4$. Interchanging horizontal and vertical directions gives equal counts for paired cases.\n$$\\begin{align*}T_8&=2\\left(\\frac{8!}{4!4!}\\right)+2\\left(\\frac{8!}{1!1!3!3!}\\right)+\\frac{8!}{2!2!2!2!}\\\\T_8&=2(70)+2(1120)+2520\\\\T_8&=4900.\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 60
          }
        ]
      }
